1
00:00:03,160 --> 00:00:04,149
Who is it?

2
00:00:05,960 --> 00:00:07,359
Well, can you see who it is?

3
00:00:07,520 --> 00:00:08,794
I'm working on it, Ben.

4
00:00:11,000 --> 00:00:12,035
She's a stripper.

5
00:00:12,520 --> 00:00:14,078
Anything you care to tell me about?

6
00:00:17,080 --> 00:00:18,229
Cover's 5 bucks, buddy.

7
00:00:18,400 --> 00:00:21,119
She takes off everything
except her shoes.

8
00:01:25,480 --> 00:01:27,948
All right, all right. Come on.

9
00:01:30,080 --> 00:01:32,640
What you waiting for, baby?

10
00:01:33,040 --> 00:01:36,112
- Take off your feather, baby.
- Yeah.

11
00:01:36,280 --> 00:01:38,350
All right.

12
00:01:38,520 --> 00:01:41,034
Come on, hurt me. Hurt me.

13
00:01:43,480 --> 00:01:46,870
- Oh, yeah, baby.
- Yeah.

14
00:01:58,880 --> 00:02:00,199
Oh, yeah.

15
00:02:21,880 --> 00:02:23,472
The lovely Yolanda,
ladies and gentlemen.

16
00:02:23,640 --> 00:02:25,198
Let's hear it for Yolanda.

17
00:02:25,680 --> 00:02:29,309
He's fine. He's reading a book.

18
00:02:30,440 --> 00:02:33,159
He's gonna be tired. Hi, mister.

19
00:02:33,320 --> 00:02:36,278
- Are you finished dancing, Mom?
- No, I have one more number.

20
00:02:36,440 --> 00:02:38,635
But Gracie and I are gonna
take you home first.

21
00:02:38,800 --> 00:02:42,110
Oh, let me stay.
Please, I'll read my book.

22
00:02:42,960 --> 00:02:46,430
- It's past your bedtime.
- I'll go to sleep here on the couch.

23
00:02:46,600 --> 00:02:49,433
Please, Mom. Please?

24
00:02:49,600 --> 00:02:50,589
Yeah?

25
00:02:51,120 --> 00:02:52,917
There's somebody here
to see you, Carla.

26
00:02:53,640 --> 00:02:54,755
Just a second.

27
00:02:54,920 --> 00:02:58,993
You get ready to go home.
I'll be right back.

28
00:02:59,960 --> 00:03:01,188
Hello, Carla.

29
00:03:02,240 --> 00:03:03,753
What are you doing here?

30
00:03:04,120 --> 00:03:07,430
You should've known I'd find you
sooner or later.

31
00:03:07,640 --> 00:03:11,599
I came by to give you a little token
of my affection.

32
00:03:16,520 --> 00:03:19,318
The process server usually does this,
but I wanted to be here in person

33
00:03:19,480 --> 00:03:23,439
- so I could see the look in your eyes.
- Another hearing. Why?

34
00:03:23,800 --> 00:03:25,870
Why can't you just let this be over?

35
00:03:26,040 --> 00:03:27,917
Well, you know why, darling.

36
00:03:28,080 --> 00:03:29,798
Because I still care.

37
00:03:31,240 --> 00:03:32,753
You're not gonna get away with it.

38
00:03:32,920 --> 00:03:35,275
That's up to the courts to decide.

39
00:03:35,440 --> 00:03:39,149
But when they see the surroundings
you're exposing my son to,

40
00:03:39,320 --> 00:03:42,039
as opposed to the advantages
Allison and I can give him--

41
00:03:42,200 --> 00:03:44,714
You know you don't give a damn
about Jimmy.

42
00:03:44,880 --> 00:03:47,269
You just want to keep punishing me.

43
00:03:47,440 --> 00:03:49,237
You know,
you seem disturbed, Carla.

44
00:03:49,400 --> 00:03:51,038
Really psychotic.

45
00:03:51,760 --> 00:03:54,115
I'm not gonna stand still for this.
I'm warning you.

46
00:03:54,280 --> 00:03:55,508
Really?

47
00:03:55,680 --> 00:03:59,309
- What are you going to do?
- Anything I have to.

48
00:04:01,080 --> 00:04:03,116
You haven't changed, have you?

49
00:04:04,120 --> 00:04:05,758
Neither have you.

50
00:04:07,120 --> 00:04:10,237
Well, I've got to run, darling.
I'll see you in court.

51
00:05:23,080 --> 00:05:25,036
Who is it?

52
00:05:43,080 --> 00:05:45,878
It was a boy. It was great.
Saw the whole thing.

53
00:05:46,040 --> 00:05:49,476
Eight pounds, 7 ounces.
Born with the fullest head of hair.

54
00:05:49,640 --> 00:05:51,710
So were you.

55
00:05:51,880 --> 00:05:54,235
Hey, say, guys.

56
00:05:55,880 --> 00:05:57,029
Well, congratulations.

57
00:05:58,880 --> 00:06:00,836
You guys are a bit of all right.

58
00:06:01,000 --> 00:06:02,911
Wanna make sure
the kid dresses better than you.

59
00:06:05,120 --> 00:06:06,189
Best to the missus.

60
00:06:06,360 --> 00:06:07,588
- Thanks, Ben.
- See you around.

61
00:06:07,760 --> 00:06:08,954
You gonna open it?

62
00:06:10,600 --> 00:06:12,318
While we're here,
we should stop by Property

63
00:06:12,480 --> 00:06:15,597
and check out the evidence
on the Morton case--

64
00:06:17,480 --> 00:06:19,357
What's the matter?

65
00:06:20,680 --> 00:06:22,033
I'll be right back.

66
00:06:22,200 --> 00:06:24,953
- Don't be shy. Take two or three.
- Sure, no problem.

67
00:06:25,120 --> 00:06:28,112
- Hey, Bob.
- That was quick.

68
00:06:28,280 --> 00:06:30,191
Cigar?

69
00:06:31,320 --> 00:06:35,472
There's a lady out there,
Carla Hardiman, used to be.

70
00:06:35,640 --> 00:06:37,596
Calls herself Evans now.

71
00:06:37,760 --> 00:06:40,228
She's the ex-wife
of Jason Hardiman,

72
00:06:40,400 --> 00:06:43,676
who, in case you hadn't heard,
was shot last night.

73
00:06:43,840 --> 00:06:46,434
He's hanging by a thread
over at County General.

74
00:06:46,600 --> 00:06:49,478
They were divorced five years ago.
What's that have to do with Carla?

75
00:06:49,640 --> 00:06:51,710
All I know is
she threatened him publicly

76
00:06:51,880 --> 00:06:55,839
just a few hours before the shooting,
so we brought her in for questioning.

77
00:06:56,000 --> 00:06:57,194
I gotta tell you something,

78
00:06:57,360 --> 00:06:59,396
if I was gonna shoot somebody,
I'd keep it a secret.

79
00:06:59,560 --> 00:07:01,790
I wouldn't yell it out
in front of a bunch of witnesses.

80
00:07:02,920 --> 00:07:05,354
Are you her lawyer?

81
00:07:05,520 --> 00:07:06,919
I'm thinking about it.

82
00:07:14,840 --> 00:07:16,512
Miss Evans,

83
00:07:16,680 --> 00:07:17,715
Ben Matlock.

84
00:07:17,880 --> 00:07:21,111
It's been a long time.
I don't know if you remember.

85
00:07:21,280 --> 00:07:22,952
I remember.

86
00:07:23,120 --> 00:07:25,475
I was just presenting
your husband's proposal.

87
00:07:25,640 --> 00:07:28,393
I was just going on what he told me.

88
00:07:28,560 --> 00:07:32,599
That I was a slut who got pregnant
so I could pry money out of him?

89
00:07:32,760 --> 00:07:35,558
Isn't that why you tried to bribe me
into giving up my baby?

90
00:07:36,000 --> 00:07:38,355
It wasn't a bribe. It was a proposal.

91
00:07:38,520 --> 00:07:40,715
It was a bribe, and you know it.

92
00:07:40,880 --> 00:07:43,348
No. And I'm sorry it appeared to be.

93
00:07:43,800 --> 00:07:46,598
Ever since I won custody of Jimmy
he's been hounding me,

94
00:07:46,760 --> 00:07:50,548
getting me fired from
one job after another.

95
00:07:50,720 --> 00:07:53,996
I finally had to change my name
and get work in a strip joint.

96
00:07:54,560 --> 00:07:57,552
Now he's found me again.
He wants to take me to court

97
00:07:57,720 --> 00:08:00,473
and have me declared an unfit mother.
Are you going to represent him?

98
00:08:01,240 --> 00:08:03,037
No. I stopped representing
your ex-husband

99
00:08:03,200 --> 00:08:06,078
when I found out what a liar he is.

100
00:08:06,240 --> 00:08:11,109
And I've always felt bad that I had
anything to do with that divorce.

101
00:08:11,280 --> 00:08:14,397
I just wanted to tell you
that if you need representation,

102
00:08:14,560 --> 00:08:17,154
I'd be happy to oblige, on the house.

103
00:08:17,320 --> 00:08:20,073
My way of apologizing.

104
00:08:21,680 --> 00:08:23,113
Can you get me out of here?

105
00:08:23,280 --> 00:08:25,236
If I'm your lawyer, yes.

106
00:08:28,720 --> 00:08:30,312
Okay.

107
00:08:33,880 --> 00:08:36,917
I'll arrange for your release.

108
00:08:43,440 --> 00:08:46,671
Ben. I got the fax from O'Hanian
after I read the sister's statement.

109
00:08:46,840 --> 00:08:49,070
It's very suspicious.

110
00:08:49,240 --> 00:08:51,959
- Where did you disappear to?
- I was hunting us up a new client.

111
00:08:52,120 --> 00:08:54,509
A new c--? The woman in the hall?

112
00:08:56,800 --> 00:09:00,031
- Who is she?
- An old acquaintance.

113
00:09:01,360 --> 00:09:03,078
Anything you care to tell me about?

114
00:09:03,240 --> 00:09:04,639
Oh, no, no.

115
00:09:04,800 --> 00:09:07,837
She was involved
in a custody case I was handling.

116
00:09:08,000 --> 00:09:09,228
A former client.

117
00:09:09,400 --> 00:09:11,550
Actually, I was representing
the husband.

118
00:09:11,720 --> 00:09:13,392
It was a very unusual case.

119
00:09:13,560 --> 00:09:15,152
- How so?
- I lost.

120
00:09:15,320 --> 00:09:19,279
- That's unusual.
- I was glad I lost.

121
00:09:21,400 --> 00:09:22,674
She's a suspect in a shooting.

122
00:09:22,840 --> 00:09:24,717
You wanna get some background?
I'll go see Bob.

123
00:09:25,520 --> 00:09:30,230
- My very thought.
- She's still a little upset with me.

124
00:09:31,600 --> 00:09:33,192
Charlene,

125
00:09:33,360 --> 00:09:34,713
she's a stripper.

126
00:10:59,200 --> 00:11:00,428
Code blue. Code blue.

127
00:11:08,560 --> 00:11:10,471
ICU 7.

128
00:11:14,800 --> 00:11:17,394
Wait a second. Stop.

129
00:11:35,000 --> 00:11:39,039
This woman first attempted to kill her
ex-husband with a handgun.

130
00:11:39,200 --> 00:11:43,796
Then, as he lay helpless in
a hospital bed, barely clinging to life,

131
00:11:43,960 --> 00:11:46,793
she entered his room
and coldly completed the job

132
00:11:46,960 --> 00:11:48,678
of snuffing out his life.

133
00:11:48,840 --> 00:11:50,910
The evidence is substantial
and compelling

134
00:11:51,080 --> 00:11:52,354
and the state strongly suspects

135
00:11:52,520 --> 00:11:54,875
that this defendant will attempt
to flee this jurisdiction

136
00:11:55,040 --> 00:11:58,191
regardless of the amount of bail set.

137
00:11:58,360 --> 00:12:02,239
We urge the court to deny bail.

138
00:12:05,240 --> 00:12:06,389
Thank you, Your Honour.

139
00:12:09,600 --> 00:12:14,549
Your Honour, to deny my client bail

140
00:12:15,520 --> 00:12:18,159
would evoke a terrible hardship.

141
00:12:18,880 --> 00:12:21,394
She's the devoted mother
of a 5-year-old son

142
00:12:21,560 --> 00:12:24,916
who needs the care and attention
only a mother can give.

143
00:12:25,960 --> 00:12:30,988
There are no other relatives
in the whole Atlanta area.

144
00:12:31,160 --> 00:12:34,470
To separate these two
and place the boy in a foster home

145
00:12:34,640 --> 00:12:36,073
would be disastrous.

146
00:12:36,240 --> 00:12:40,791
I earnestly beg the court to consider
the boy in rendering its decision.

147
00:12:40,960 --> 00:12:43,793
I think a reasonable bail
is appropriate.

148
00:12:46,160 --> 00:12:51,109
Thank you for your eloquent advice,
Mr. Matlock, but I'm going to deny bail.

149
00:12:56,880 --> 00:12:58,313
I'm sorry.

150
00:13:02,400 --> 00:13:04,516
Tell Jimmy...

151
00:13:05,320 --> 00:13:06,958
...I had to take a trip.

152
00:13:07,400 --> 00:13:09,072
Gracie knows how to take care of him.

153
00:13:09,240 --> 00:13:10,798
You sure you don't
wanna see him first?

154
00:13:11,760 --> 00:13:14,274
Not like this.

155
00:13:14,440 --> 00:13:17,034
Yeah, it looks like
she came in this way.

156
00:13:17,200 --> 00:13:19,031
High-heel marks
in the grass over there.

157
00:13:19,200 --> 00:13:21,111
Yeah.

158
00:13:21,760 --> 00:13:24,069
- She went in through that door.
- Yeah. Forced it.

159
00:13:24,240 --> 00:13:27,710
- Pretty strong woman.
- Yeah. Apparently.

160
00:13:29,640 --> 00:13:32,313
- Excuse me a minute, Bob.
- Sure.

161
00:13:32,480 --> 00:13:34,198
I want you to check
the lower windows

162
00:13:34,360 --> 00:13:36,476
as well as the door
for prints, all right?

163
00:13:36,640 --> 00:13:39,154
Morning, Tyler.

164
00:13:39,320 --> 00:13:40,309
What's this?

165
00:13:40,480 --> 00:13:43,995
Ben, there are several kinds
of whizzes in this world.

166
00:13:44,160 --> 00:13:47,516
Now, the kind of whiz that I am
is a stock-market whiz.

167
00:13:47,680 --> 00:13:50,240
- What's he talking about?
- He says he's gonna retire next week.

168
00:13:50,400 --> 00:13:53,995
Red, turbo-charged,
2.8 multi-faceted,

169
00:13:54,160 --> 00:13:57,755
fuel-injected convertible car
with cellular phone

170
00:13:57,920 --> 00:14:00,878
is the results of profits
from one day's playing

171
00:14:01,040 --> 00:14:03,634
- the open stock market.
- One day?

172
00:14:03,800 --> 00:14:05,631
One day.
So when you see me coming--

173
00:14:05,800 --> 00:14:08,109
- Here comes the whiz?
- Here comes the whiz.

174
00:14:08,280 --> 00:14:10,999
And my stock is
at 73 and still climbing.

175
00:14:12,880 --> 00:14:14,233
No more surveillance.

176
00:14:14,400 --> 00:14:15,879
No more subpoenas.

177
00:14:16,040 --> 00:14:18,679
No more stakeouts.

178
00:14:19,440 --> 00:14:21,158
Well, Tyler, I'm gonna miss you.

179
00:14:24,000 --> 00:14:26,036
Picking over the peaches,
are you, Ben?

180
00:14:26,200 --> 00:14:27,872
Morning, Allison.

181
00:14:32,160 --> 00:14:34,230
What is it?

182
00:14:34,400 --> 00:14:38,757
I just wanted to convey
my condolences.

183
00:14:40,400 --> 00:14:41,879
Thank you.

184
00:14:43,240 --> 00:14:46,152
Allison, I have to ask you
some questions.

185
00:14:46,320 --> 00:14:48,231
I know this is a difficult time for you,

186
00:14:48,400 --> 00:14:51,233
- but it's my job.
- What do you wanna know, Ben?

187
00:14:54,400 --> 00:14:58,279
How did Jason find out where
Carla Evans was working?

188
00:14:59,920 --> 00:15:01,638
I think somebody told him.

189
00:15:01,800 --> 00:15:04,109
Oh, yes. I remember.
He got a telephone call

190
00:15:04,280 --> 00:15:05,679
from someone
who worked at her...

191
00:15:07,360 --> 00:15:09,510
...club.

192
00:15:12,320 --> 00:15:13,878
He really wanted that boy, didn't he?

193
00:15:14,040 --> 00:15:17,350
Once he owned something,
he never liked to part with it.

194
00:15:20,640 --> 00:15:22,119
Anything else?

195
00:15:23,520 --> 00:15:25,795
Oh, I don't know, Allison.
I'm embarrassed to ask.

196
00:15:25,960 --> 00:15:28,599
Never stopped you before.

197
00:15:30,640 --> 00:15:32,392
According to the police records,

198
00:15:32,560 --> 00:15:35,518
you weren't at home
when your husband was shot.

199
00:15:35,680 --> 00:15:38,319
I drove up to our cabin
at Lake Lenier.

200
00:15:39,200 --> 00:15:42,237
- Alone?
- Yes, alone.

201
00:15:43,160 --> 00:15:45,355
All by yourself
in the middle of the night?

202
00:15:46,120 --> 00:15:48,156
Yes.

203
00:15:49,920 --> 00:15:51,797
Wayne can confirm that.

204
00:15:51,960 --> 00:15:55,953
Wayne is the caretaker
at our place on the lake.

205
00:15:56,320 --> 00:15:58,959
Mr. Matlock wants to know
if I was at the lake

206
00:15:59,120 --> 00:16:00,792
all night Wednesday.

207
00:16:00,960 --> 00:16:02,598
She was.

208
00:16:03,880 --> 00:16:05,996
Bye, Ben.

209
00:16:06,560 --> 00:16:08,630
Bye, Allison.

210
00:16:10,960 --> 00:16:15,112
Tyler, I want you to keep a sharp eye
on Allison Hardiman.

211
00:16:16,280 --> 00:16:17,474
What's the matter?

212
00:16:17,640 --> 00:16:19,517
I don't know.
It just seems kind of sad.

213
00:16:20,000 --> 00:16:20,989
What?

214
00:16:21,160 --> 00:16:22,752
My last stakeout.

215
00:16:27,040 --> 00:16:29,600
- So, what do you think?
- About Tyler?

216
00:16:29,760 --> 00:16:32,035
No, I mean about this.

217
00:16:32,200 --> 00:16:33,189
I don't know, Charlene.

218
00:16:33,360 --> 00:16:35,555
I've known Allison Hardiman
a long time.

219
00:16:36,120 --> 00:16:39,510
It's hard to imagine she went through
all this rigmarole to shoot Jason.

220
00:16:40,640 --> 00:16:43,837
Well, I think I'll go over to the hospital
and nose around.

221
00:16:44,000 --> 00:16:45,752
Good idea.

222
00:16:48,400 --> 00:16:52,154
- Nurse Jackson?
- Yes.

223
00:16:52,320 --> 00:16:55,995
Are you the nurse
who identified Carla Evans?

224
00:16:56,160 --> 00:16:58,037
Yes. Are you from the newspaper?

225
00:16:58,200 --> 00:17:00,634
No. I'm sorry, I'm Charlene Matlock.

226
00:17:00,800 --> 00:17:02,791
I'm an attorney
representing Carla Evans.

227
00:17:02,960 --> 00:17:05,269
Then I have nothing to say.

228
00:17:08,800 --> 00:17:11,030
Well, you had a great deal
to say to the police.

229
00:17:11,200 --> 00:17:13,430
That's right.

230
00:17:14,760 --> 00:17:15,988
For someone to come in here,

231
00:17:16,160 --> 00:17:19,470
to endanger the lives of all of
our patients, murder one of them.

232
00:17:19,640 --> 00:17:22,950
How could you defend
someone like that?

233
00:17:28,520 --> 00:17:31,398
Sometimes it isn't easy.

234
00:17:32,160 --> 00:17:36,233
Your case hangs on this videotape
of a hospital security camera

235
00:17:36,400 --> 00:17:38,630
and the nurse
who saw the killer leave.

236
00:17:38,800 --> 00:17:40,870
Anybody you know?

237
00:17:41,040 --> 00:17:42,678
Someone I know?

238
00:17:42,840 --> 00:17:45,991
Yeah, somebody you know
who doesn't like you very much.

239
00:17:46,160 --> 00:17:49,630
Somebody told Jason Hardiman
where you were.

240
00:17:49,800 --> 00:17:51,950
I'm sorry.

241
00:17:52,120 --> 00:17:54,270
I don't recognize her.

242
00:17:54,440 --> 00:17:58,433
Well, if it's not you,
it's somebody made up to look like you.

243
00:17:59,960 --> 00:18:01,996
What about Jason's wife, Allison?

244
00:18:02,160 --> 00:18:03,912
We're checking her out.

245
00:18:05,440 --> 00:18:08,876
- Anybody else?
- I don't know.

246
00:18:09,600 --> 00:18:10,999
Maybe Helen.

247
00:18:11,560 --> 00:18:12,549
Who's Helen?

248
00:18:13,200 --> 00:18:15,589
Helen Shelly.
She was a friend of Doug Templitt,

249
00:18:15,760 --> 00:18:17,671
the emcee at the club
where I worked.

250
00:18:17,840 --> 00:18:19,831
She got it into her head
that I was after Doug,

251
00:18:20,000 --> 00:18:22,878
which was ridiculous because there
was nothing going on between us.

252
00:18:23,040 --> 00:18:29,559
But anyway, she would call me up
every night for about a week.

253
00:18:29,720 --> 00:18:31,039
She'd threaten me.

254
00:18:32,160 --> 00:18:36,312
I told her I'd call the cops
if she didn't stop, so she stopped.

255
00:18:36,480 --> 00:18:38,948
- I'll check her out.
- I didn't take her seriously.

256
00:18:39,120 --> 00:18:41,588
Besides, this was a month ago or so.

257
00:18:41,760 --> 00:18:43,193
I haven't seen or heard of her since.

258
00:18:44,800 --> 00:18:45,789
Doug Templitt?

259
00:18:46,800 --> 00:18:48,791
Yeah.

260
00:18:57,520 --> 00:18:58,748
Cover's 5 bucks, buddy.

261
00:18:58,920 --> 00:19:01,718
She takes off everything
except her shoes.

262
00:19:02,120 --> 00:19:04,759
She doesn't take off her shoes?

263
00:19:34,880 --> 00:19:36,711
The lovely Sabrina,
ladies and gentlemen.

264
00:19:36,880 --> 00:19:38,598
Let's hear it for Sabrina.

265
00:19:40,200 --> 00:19:42,270
A little while ago,
I was over at the bar

266
00:19:42,440 --> 00:19:45,000
and a woman walked in
with a duck under her arm.

267
00:19:45,160 --> 00:19:47,674
Harry, our bartender,
he walks over to her and he says,

268
00:19:47,840 --> 00:19:49,796
''What are you doing with the pig?''

269
00:19:49,960 --> 00:19:52,269
The woman says, ''It's a duck.''

270
00:19:52,440 --> 00:19:55,079
Harry says,
''I was talking to the duck.''

271
00:19:57,360 --> 00:19:58,873
I'm gonna call Forest Lawn for you.

272
00:19:59,040 --> 00:20:01,554
How about a big hand for
our wonderful orchestra over there.

273
00:20:01,720 --> 00:20:04,393
Don't they sound terrific tonight?
Don't they?

274
00:20:05,600 --> 00:20:09,434
She was spitting bullets the night
that Hardiman came by to see her.

275
00:20:09,600 --> 00:20:11,113
You heard the conversation?

276
00:20:11,280 --> 00:20:14,716
Yes, and I will testify. I'm her friend.

277
00:20:16,560 --> 00:20:18,755
She needs all the friends she can get.

278
00:20:18,920 --> 00:20:21,229
Right now, it's her enemies
I'm interested in.

279
00:20:21,680 --> 00:20:23,636
And I think

280
00:20:23,800 --> 00:20:26,519
somebody who knew Jason Hardiman
was looking for her

281
00:20:26,680 --> 00:20:28,432
and was willing to tell him
where she was.

282
00:20:28,600 --> 00:20:30,318
Well, who would do anything like that?

283
00:20:32,280 --> 00:20:34,840
That's what I'd sure like to find out.

284
00:20:35,000 --> 00:20:37,798
- Who are you?
- I'm her lawyer, Ben Matlock.

285
00:20:37,960 --> 00:20:40,872
I'm on Carla's side, so if there's
anything at all that I can do to help--

286
00:20:41,040 --> 00:20:43,952
You can tell me how Jason Hardiman
knew she was working here.

287
00:20:45,320 --> 00:20:48,153
Well, nobody here would do that.
We're all friends here.

288
00:20:48,320 --> 00:20:51,596
Carla said you have a friend
named Helen Shelly.

289
00:20:52,480 --> 00:20:54,311
She couldn't have had
anything to do with it.

290
00:20:54,480 --> 00:20:55,879
How can you be sure?

291
00:20:56,040 --> 00:20:57,712
I haven't seen her in months.

292
00:20:58,080 --> 00:20:59,433
I need to find her.

293
00:21:00,880 --> 00:21:01,949
I don't know.

294
00:21:03,240 --> 00:21:04,389
Well, I have to find her.

295
00:21:04,560 --> 00:21:07,677
There's an easy way and a hard way.
Either way, I have to find her.

296
00:21:07,840 --> 00:21:09,159
Here's my card.

297
00:21:09,320 --> 00:21:12,756
In case she contacts you,
have her give me a call.

298
00:21:12,920 --> 00:21:15,388
Thank you both for your help.

299
00:21:26,120 --> 00:21:27,599
No, no, no, I'm not worried.

300
00:21:27,760 --> 00:21:29,910
I was worried two hours ago.
Now I'm frantic.

301
00:21:30,080 --> 00:21:33,595
Just get me out of it, okay?
Just sell it. Yeah, sell.

302
00:21:33,760 --> 00:21:36,354
Hold on, hold on.
I got somebody on the other line.

303
00:21:38,000 --> 00:21:39,513
Hello?

304
00:21:39,680 --> 00:21:42,148
<i>Tyler, I've been trying to reach you.</i>

305
00:21:42,320 --> 00:21:43,878
Your line's always busy.

306
00:21:44,040 --> 00:21:45,712
Ben, let me get
right back to you, okay?

307
00:21:47,000 --> 00:21:50,788
Now, look, Irv. I gotta go.
Just sell everything, okay?

308
00:21:50,960 --> 00:21:53,155
No, I don't care.
Just get what you can.

309
00:21:53,320 --> 00:21:55,709
And call me back. I'll be in my car.

310
00:21:55,880 --> 00:21:57,359
All right.

311
00:21:58,120 --> 00:21:59,553
All right.

312
00:21:59,720 --> 00:22:00,709
Yes, Ben?

313
00:22:01,160 --> 00:22:03,833
Tyler, what's going on
with Allison Hardiman?

314
00:22:04,000 --> 00:22:05,638
I followed her to the Red Embers.

315
00:22:05,800 --> 00:22:07,392
I figured she was gonna
meet somebody.

316
00:22:07,560 --> 00:22:11,155
She's been acting suspicious,
I think she's trying to lose me.

317
00:22:15,280 --> 00:22:16,918
How is that for timing?

318
00:22:21,880 --> 00:22:24,599
- There she goes.
- Well, follow her.

319
00:22:24,760 --> 00:22:25,988
All right.

320
00:22:31,240 --> 00:22:33,071
<i>Tyler?</i>

321
00:22:33,240 --> 00:22:34,992
<i>Tyler?</i>

322
00:22:35,560 --> 00:22:36,959
Tyler, what's happening?

323
00:22:37,120 --> 00:22:39,839
<i>- I'm still following her, Ben.</i>
- Well, don't lose her.

324
00:22:40,000 --> 00:22:42,355
Do you tell Julia Child
how to fry an egg?

325
00:22:42,520 --> 00:22:44,431
Is she with somebody?
Can you see?

326
00:22:44,600 --> 00:22:46,875
- Not yet.
<i>- Get closer.</i>

327
00:22:47,040 --> 00:22:49,315
- I'm trying.
<i>- Can you see who it is?</i>

328
00:22:49,480 --> 00:22:50,833
I'm working on it, Ben.

329
00:22:51,000 --> 00:22:54,117
I'm gonna take this shortcut through
the alley, try to get in front in her.

330
00:22:54,560 --> 00:22:56,437
<i>Tyler?</i>

331
00:22:56,600 --> 00:22:58,272
<i>Tyler?</i>

332
00:22:58,440 --> 00:22:59,953
<i>Tyler?</i>

333
00:23:01,760 --> 00:23:03,671
Tyler?

334
00:23:05,120 --> 00:23:06,109
Tyler.

335
00:23:07,680 --> 00:23:10,478
<i>- Tyler, are you all right?</i>
- Yeah, I'm fine,

336
00:23:10,960 --> 00:23:13,679
but I think I lost them momentarily.

337
00:23:29,840 --> 00:23:31,512
- Did you check that plate number?
- Yeah.

338
00:23:31,680 --> 00:23:34,433
The car is registered
to Mrs. Hardiman.

339
00:23:34,600 --> 00:23:37,797
You better get up to their lake house,
have a talk with Wayne Cornell.

340
00:23:37,960 --> 00:23:40,190
He's the caretaker.

341
00:23:41,120 --> 00:23:43,429
- What's the matter?
- No car.

342
00:23:48,680 --> 00:23:49,669
Take mine.

343
00:23:52,280 --> 00:23:56,637
Ben, I've been thinking.
Allison Hardiman could be the one.

344
00:23:56,800 --> 00:23:58,472
She's close in height
and build to Carla.

345
00:23:58,640 --> 00:24:00,756
Put a red wig on her
and she matches the description.

346
00:24:00,920 --> 00:24:04,196
- Yeah.
- Well, what are the alternatives?

347
00:24:04,360 --> 00:24:08,558
There's Allison Hardiman,
there's Carla's friend, Gracie,

348
00:24:09,160 --> 00:24:12,436
there's this mystery woman, Helen.

349
00:24:13,240 --> 00:24:16,198
There's Carla herself.
Is that what you're thinking?

350
00:24:18,440 --> 00:24:20,271
Hello?

351
00:24:22,480 --> 00:24:23,708
It's Helen.

352
00:24:25,440 --> 00:24:28,591
Yes? This is Ben Matlock.

353
00:24:29,640 --> 00:24:31,358
Yeah.

354
00:24:33,320 --> 00:24:35,390
Yes, I'll be there.

355
00:24:51,520 --> 00:24:52,839
- Miss Shelly?
- Yes.

356
00:24:53,000 --> 00:24:53,989
Ben Matlock.

357
00:24:54,680 --> 00:24:56,671
- Hello.
- Thank you for seeing me.

358
00:24:56,840 --> 00:24:57,955
Of course.

359
00:24:58,680 --> 00:25:00,910
- Would you care for a drink?
- No, thank you.

360
00:25:01,080 --> 00:25:03,116
I must tell you, Mr. Matlock,

361
00:25:03,280 --> 00:25:05,635
Doug really didn't want me
to speak to you.

362
00:25:06,720 --> 00:25:09,029
- You're still friends?
- Oh, yes.

363
00:25:09,200 --> 00:25:11,714
Doug said you hadn't seen
one another in quite a while.

364
00:25:12,240 --> 00:25:13,912
But we're still friends.

365
00:25:15,560 --> 00:25:17,312
Then you must know Carla Evans.

366
00:25:17,480 --> 00:25:19,391
No, not really.

367
00:25:20,320 --> 00:25:24,552
She said you called her. Often.
Says you threatened her.

368
00:25:24,720 --> 00:25:26,756
Threatened her?

369
00:25:26,920 --> 00:25:29,150
I've never even spoken to her.

370
00:25:31,160 --> 00:25:34,038
- You know Jason Hardiman?
- Who?

371
00:25:34,200 --> 00:25:36,509
Carla's ex-husband.
She's been accused of murdering him.

372
00:25:37,040 --> 00:25:39,429
Mr. Matlock, what has all this
got to do with me?

373
00:25:39,600 --> 00:25:43,036
I don't know that it has
anything to do with you.

374
00:25:44,080 --> 00:25:46,150
I have a strong suspicion

375
00:25:46,320 --> 00:25:49,118
that another woman impersonating
Carla committed the murder.

376
00:25:49,280 --> 00:25:52,511
Somebody who had reason to hate her
and maybe wanted to get even.

377
00:25:52,680 --> 00:25:54,398
You're not suggesting
I had to do with it.

378
00:25:54,560 --> 00:25:57,472
- Oh, no. I'm not suggesting anything.
- Good.

379
00:25:57,640 --> 00:25:58,868
Then don't.

380
00:26:00,200 --> 00:26:02,839
I'll tell you what Carla is,
Mr. Matlock.

381
00:26:03,680 --> 00:26:05,079
Carla is a liar.

382
00:26:08,360 --> 00:26:10,510
Excuse me.

383
00:26:13,320 --> 00:26:15,675
- Are you all right?
- I'm fine.

384
00:26:16,320 --> 00:26:17,833
Let me get something for that.

385
00:26:18,000 --> 00:26:20,355
- No, no, no, really.
- Be right back.

386
00:26:20,520 --> 00:26:24,229
Excuse me, do you have--? The lady
cut her hand. Something for her...

387
00:26:37,520 --> 00:26:41,718
Miss Jackson, is this the same person
you saw leaving Mr. Hardiman's room

388
00:26:41,880 --> 00:26:44,872
moments after
his life-support monitors went flat?

389
00:26:45,040 --> 00:26:46,871
Yes, sir. It is.

390
00:26:47,040 --> 00:26:48,519
Would you look around
the courtroom

391
00:26:48,680 --> 00:26:50,636
and tell us if that person
is present today?

392
00:26:51,480 --> 00:26:52,754
That person right there.

393
00:26:54,320 --> 00:26:59,155
May the record show the witness
has identified the defendant.

394
00:26:59,840 --> 00:27:02,479
The records will so indicate.

395
00:27:03,120 --> 00:27:04,599
I have no further questions.

396
00:27:04,760 --> 00:27:05,988
Cross-examine?

397
00:27:12,520 --> 00:27:15,193
It's nice to see you again,
Miss Jackson.

398
00:27:18,200 --> 00:27:21,192
- Why do you wear glasses?
- I'm nearsighted.

399
00:27:22,000 --> 00:27:25,310
So you wear them so that
you can see things in the distance.

400
00:27:26,760 --> 00:27:28,990
Yes, and I see perfectly with them.

401
00:27:29,480 --> 00:27:31,391
Good.

402
00:27:31,560 --> 00:27:33,232
Miss Jackson,
were you wearing your glasses

403
00:27:33,400 --> 00:27:36,358
when you identified Carla Evans
just now?

404
00:27:36,520 --> 00:27:38,795
- Yes.
- Were you also wearing them

405
00:27:38,960 --> 00:27:41,190
when you viewed
the security videotape?

406
00:27:41,360 --> 00:27:42,759
Yes.

407
00:27:43,680 --> 00:27:47,116
So you were wearing them when
you saw the woman in the hospital.

408
00:27:47,280 --> 00:27:49,077
Yes, I was.

409
00:27:51,280 --> 00:27:54,238
Let's look at the videotape again.

410
00:27:54,400 --> 00:27:57,312
I call your attention to the part
after the woman has run away.

411
00:27:59,520 --> 00:28:01,112
Miss Jackson, that's you, isn't it,

412
00:28:01,280 --> 00:28:02,872
when you observed
the woman running away?

413
00:28:03,040 --> 00:28:04,359
Yes, it is.

414
00:28:06,280 --> 00:28:09,352
Miss Jackson,
you're not wearing your glasses.

415
00:28:15,360 --> 00:28:17,078
Well, in the confusion,
I suppose I might--

416
00:28:17,240 --> 00:28:20,630
I can understand how you might have
thought you had your glasses on,

417
00:28:20,800 --> 00:28:23,189
just as you thought the woman
in the hallway was Carla Evans.

418
00:28:23,360 --> 00:28:25,316
But you couldn't really see her,
could you?

419
00:28:32,960 --> 00:28:34,632
I don't know. I'm not sure.

420
00:28:36,560 --> 00:28:39,074
No further questions, Your Honour.

421
00:28:40,000 --> 00:28:40,989
Redirect?

422
00:28:42,400 --> 00:28:45,198
No, Your Honour. The people rest.

423
00:28:45,360 --> 00:28:47,271
Miss Jackson, you may step down.

424
00:28:47,440 --> 00:28:50,273
You nailed that one, didn't you?

425
00:28:58,440 --> 00:29:00,874
Your Honour, if it pleases the court,

426
00:29:01,040 --> 00:29:04,794
the defence would like to call as
its first witness Mr. Wayne Cornell.

427
00:29:06,040 --> 00:29:08,873
Mr. Cornell, how long
have you been caretaker

428
00:29:09,040 --> 00:29:10,917
of the Hardimans' lake house?

429
00:29:11,080 --> 00:29:12,672
Two years.

430
00:29:12,840 --> 00:29:17,595
Did anybody visit the lake house
the night Jason Hardiman was shot?

431
00:29:17,760 --> 00:29:20,718
- Mrs. Hardiman came up that night.
- She did?

432
00:29:20,880 --> 00:29:23,917
- Was anybody with her?
- No, she was by herself.

433
00:29:24,080 --> 00:29:27,390
Well, were you there?
Did you see her arrive?

434
00:29:27,560 --> 00:29:29,915
I saw her arrive.
I saw her leave the next morning.

435
00:29:30,080 --> 00:29:31,559
Irrelevant, Your Honour.

436
00:29:31,720 --> 00:29:33,950
Mrs. Hardiman is not on trial here.

437
00:29:34,120 --> 00:29:36,111
Mr. Matlock,
just where is this going?

438
00:29:36,280 --> 00:29:38,669
A few more questions, Your Honour,
and it'll become evident.

439
00:29:38,840 --> 00:29:41,752
Very well, but kindly get to the point
as quickly as you can.

440
00:29:41,920 --> 00:29:43,353
Yes, sir.

441
00:29:43,520 --> 00:29:46,239
Mr. Cornell, how do you know

442
00:29:46,400 --> 00:29:50,279
that Mrs. Hardiman
was there all night that night?

443
00:29:50,440 --> 00:29:53,034
Well, for one thing,
her car was parked outside.

444
00:29:53,200 --> 00:29:55,316
But did you see her in the house?

445
00:29:56,400 --> 00:29:58,595
No, but I saw the light go on
in her bedroom window.

446
00:29:58,760 --> 00:29:59,875
Did you see the light go off

447
00:30:00,040 --> 00:30:01,439
- in her bedroom window?
- Yeah.

448
00:30:03,560 --> 00:30:05,312
- That's how you knew she was there.
- Right.

449
00:30:05,480 --> 00:30:08,472
Good, good, good.
Now we're getting somewhere.

450
00:30:08,640 --> 00:30:10,915
Were you there September 2nd?

451
00:30:11,080 --> 00:30:12,513
Oh, I'm there all year round.

452
00:30:13,080 --> 00:30:15,514
Do you recall
having a visitor that day?

453
00:30:17,160 --> 00:30:18,752
No, I don't remember.

454
00:30:19,440 --> 00:30:21,749
Gee, it hadn't been that long ago.

455
00:30:21,920 --> 00:30:23,592
Let me see if I can help.

456
00:30:23,760 --> 00:30:25,990
It was the Tuesday after Labor Day

457
00:30:26,160 --> 00:30:29,152
and the Hardimans
had closed up the house,

458
00:30:29,320 --> 00:30:31,197
and the man
from the power company

459
00:30:31,360 --> 00:30:34,352
came up there like he does
every year after Labor Day.

460
00:30:34,520 --> 00:30:37,478
Now, does that help you
with your recollection?

461
00:30:38,760 --> 00:30:39,749
Yes.

462
00:30:41,040 --> 00:30:44,589
So the man from the power company
was there that day.

463
00:30:44,760 --> 00:30:46,398
Yeah.

464
00:30:46,560 --> 00:30:48,516
What did he do?

465
00:30:48,680 --> 00:30:50,557
- Shut off the electricity.
- Say again?

466
00:30:50,720 --> 00:30:53,188
He shut off the electricity.

467
00:30:54,480 --> 00:30:55,708
I see.

468
00:30:55,880 --> 00:30:58,758
Mr. Cornell, you've testified

469
00:30:58,920 --> 00:31:01,115
that Mrs. Hardiman
was at the lake house

470
00:31:01,280 --> 00:31:03,669
the night of the shooting
and that you saw the lights

471
00:31:03,840 --> 00:31:07,435
go on and off in her bedroom.
That's not quite true, is it?

472
00:31:08,200 --> 00:31:09,189
No.

473
00:31:09,360 --> 00:31:13,717
Mrs. Hardiman was not
at the lake house that night, was she?

474
00:31:18,440 --> 00:31:19,429
No.

475
00:31:19,600 --> 00:31:24,833
Mrs. Hardiman told you to say she was
at the lake house that night, didn't she?

476
00:31:27,560 --> 00:31:28,788
Yes.

477
00:31:29,640 --> 00:31:31,790
No further questions.

478
00:31:31,960 --> 00:31:35,839
- Mr. Hawkins?
- I have no questions, Your Honour.

479
00:31:36,000 --> 00:31:38,753
You can step down, Mr. Cornell.

480
00:31:39,160 --> 00:31:42,277
Your Honour,
I call Allison Hardiman to the stand.

481
00:31:42,840 --> 00:31:44,558
Mrs. Hardiman,

482
00:31:45,240 --> 00:31:47,913
you are the chief beneficiary
of your husband's will,

483
00:31:48,080 --> 00:31:50,036
- is that correct?
- Yes, I am.

484
00:31:50,200 --> 00:31:54,273
And as a result of his death,
you've inherited several million dollars,

485
00:31:54,440 --> 00:31:56,635
- is that correct?
- I believe so.

486
00:31:56,800 --> 00:32:01,669
Mrs. Hardiman, do you know
what ''subornation of perjury'' means?

487
00:32:02,400 --> 00:32:03,389
No.

488
00:32:05,520 --> 00:32:10,310
It means getting someone to lie
for you under oath,

489
00:32:10,920 --> 00:32:13,354
and it's a very serious offence.

490
00:32:14,040 --> 00:32:17,589
Now, your caretaker has testified
that you asked him

491
00:32:17,760 --> 00:32:22,276
to lie for you about the night
your husband was shot.

492
00:32:26,080 --> 00:32:28,275
We're trying the charge
of murder here.

493
00:32:29,440 --> 00:32:32,193
My client's life is at stake,

494
00:32:32,360 --> 00:32:35,318
and I refuse to allow her
to be convicted unjustly

495
00:32:35,480 --> 00:32:37,869
as a result of perjured testimony.

496
00:32:38,040 --> 00:32:40,918
I want you to tell this court
about that night,

497
00:32:41,080 --> 00:32:44,197
what you did and where you went.

498
00:32:44,360 --> 00:32:47,955
And I serve notice that this time
only the truth will do.

499
00:32:55,120 --> 00:32:57,111
I was--

500
00:32:58,840 --> 00:33:00,956
I was with another man.

501
00:33:02,400 --> 00:33:03,958
- Another man?
- Yes.

502
00:33:04,120 --> 00:33:07,192
- What man?
- James O'Donnell.

503
00:33:09,240 --> 00:33:10,673
That's your late husband's

504
00:33:10,840 --> 00:33:12,432
- business partner, isn't it?
- Yes.

505
00:33:13,240 --> 00:33:14,832
Where were you
and Mr. O'Donnell?

506
00:33:15,000 --> 00:33:17,230
At the Turner Arms.

507
00:33:17,400 --> 00:33:20,437
I registered in my name.

508
00:33:20,600 --> 00:33:22,511
I was afraid it might come to this.

509
00:33:22,680 --> 00:33:25,513
Here's the hotel bill.

510
00:33:28,080 --> 00:33:30,150
I see.

511
00:33:31,360 --> 00:33:34,557
So the reason you lied under oath

512
00:33:34,720 --> 00:33:37,712
and encouraged others
to do the same,

513
00:33:37,880 --> 00:33:41,111
the reason you jeopardized
my client's life and liberty

514
00:33:41,280 --> 00:33:43,669
was to conceal the fact
that you were having an affair.

515
00:33:43,840 --> 00:33:45,034
- Is that correct?
- Yes.

516
00:33:46,880 --> 00:33:48,552
But that doesn't mean I killed
my husband,

517
00:33:48,720 --> 00:33:50,870
because I didn't.

518
00:33:54,760 --> 00:33:56,830
No further questions.

519
00:34:01,200 --> 00:34:05,159
Well, we had one halfway decent
suspect, Allison Hardiman.

520
00:34:05,320 --> 00:34:06,719
Now we don't have her.

521
00:34:06,880 --> 00:34:09,713
Well, someone had to be made up
to look like me on that tape.

522
00:34:09,880 --> 00:34:11,836
Something's gnawing at me.

523
00:34:12,000 --> 00:34:15,436
I don't know what it is,
but it's driving me crazy.

524
00:34:15,600 --> 00:34:18,398
Is there more to this? Is there
something you haven't told me?

525
00:34:22,480 --> 00:34:24,277
You never did believe me, did you?

526
00:34:27,000 --> 00:34:29,673
Well, then just get out.
Come on, get out.

527
00:34:30,240 --> 00:34:32,151
I'm not gonna walk out on you.

528
00:34:34,320 --> 00:34:37,312
Is there anything or anybody
we've overlooked?

529
00:34:39,120 --> 00:34:40,473
I don't know.

530
00:34:41,800 --> 00:34:44,872
I don't either.
I'll see you in the morning.

531
00:34:55,000 --> 00:34:58,959
Irv, I don't care. I want you to sell
everything at the opening bell.

532
00:34:59,120 --> 00:35:01,953
Right, tomorrow.

533
00:35:03,760 --> 00:35:05,034
I don't believe it.

534
00:35:05,200 --> 00:35:08,317
The biggest bull market
of my lifetime and I'm ruined.

535
00:35:08,480 --> 00:35:11,392
Why don't you go home
and get some sleep?

536
00:35:12,120 --> 00:35:16,033
Yeah, might as well get used to doing
things that don't cost money.

537
00:35:16,440 --> 00:35:18,476
See you tomorrow.

538
00:35:43,560 --> 00:35:47,633
If you're not gonna get some sleep,
then at least stay awake in style.

539
00:35:47,800 --> 00:35:50,030
- Thanks.
- It's my own private blend.

540
00:35:51,440 --> 00:35:53,158
I've been trying to track down
Helen Shelly,

541
00:35:53,320 --> 00:35:55,834
but so far nothing.

542
00:36:05,200 --> 00:36:09,716
Well, I think I'm gonna
get some sleep.

543
00:36:13,880 --> 00:36:15,996
I'll see you tomorrow.

544
00:36:16,160 --> 00:36:17,957
Charlene?

545
00:36:18,120 --> 00:36:20,634
Unbutton your jacket.

546
00:36:24,680 --> 00:36:25,954
Now button it.

547
00:36:29,720 --> 00:36:30,869
Something wrong?

548
00:36:35,200 --> 00:36:37,430
I don't know.

549
00:36:39,400 --> 00:36:41,550
- See you tomorrow.
- Yeah.

550
00:36:50,960 --> 00:36:52,791
Hello?

551
00:36:54,920 --> 00:36:55,909
Hello?

552
00:36:58,520 --> 00:37:00,351
Anybody here?

553
00:37:00,520 --> 00:37:02,272
Mr. Matlock?

554
00:37:02,440 --> 00:37:04,158
What do you want?

555
00:37:04,320 --> 00:37:07,630
- I need to see Helen.
- Well, what are you asking me for?

556
00:37:07,800 --> 00:37:10,155
- I don't know where she is.
- I have to find her.

557
00:37:10,320 --> 00:37:12,276
Well, that's your problem.

558
00:37:14,880 --> 00:37:17,838
Then I'll have the marshals
find her, Doug.

559
00:37:18,000 --> 00:37:19,797
What? What do you mean?

560
00:37:19,960 --> 00:37:23,111
The court has issued a subpoena
for Helen to appear at trial tomorrow.

561
00:37:23,280 --> 00:37:26,909
If she doesn't show up,
we'll find her no matter where she is.

562
00:37:27,080 --> 00:37:30,914
If you're a friend of hers,
you'll get word to her right away. Fast.

563
00:37:33,360 --> 00:37:37,353
I'll try and find her.
I don't know that she'll listen to me.

564
00:37:37,520 --> 00:37:38,589
I'll try.

565
00:37:40,120 --> 00:37:42,270
You do that.

566
00:37:49,400 --> 00:37:52,949
Look around out there and see
if you can see her, will you? Quick.

567
00:37:55,000 --> 00:37:58,515
Miss Fielder, how long
have you known Carla Evans?

568
00:37:58,680 --> 00:38:00,432
About a year.

569
00:38:01,280 --> 00:38:03,032
And were you present
when the victim appeared

570
00:38:03,200 --> 00:38:05,919
at the Tassels nightclub
on the 1 8th of this month?

571
00:38:06,080 --> 00:38:07,479
Yes.

572
00:38:10,480 --> 00:38:14,234
Do you recall what was said between
Carla Evans and the decedent?

573
00:38:14,400 --> 00:38:15,913
Yes, I do.

574
00:38:16,080 --> 00:38:18,878
And did Miss Evans at any time
threaten the decedent?

575
00:38:19,040 --> 00:38:21,838
No. No.

576
00:38:30,080 --> 00:38:31,069
Thank you, Miss Fielder.

577
00:38:31,480 --> 00:38:34,790
I have no further questions
for this witness, Your Honour.

578
00:38:35,040 --> 00:38:37,713
Mrs. Fielder, you may step down.

579
00:38:37,880 --> 00:38:40,269
Your Honour,

580
00:38:40,440 --> 00:38:44,399
at this time, defence would like to call
Miss Helen Shelly.

581
00:38:45,480 --> 00:38:47,789
Miss Shelly,

582
00:38:47,960 --> 00:38:51,396
do you know the defendant,
Carla Evans?

583
00:38:51,560 --> 00:38:53,596
I know her slightly.

584
00:38:53,760 --> 00:38:56,069
Have you ever met her?

585
00:38:56,680 --> 00:38:58,477
I've seen her before.

586
00:38:58,640 --> 00:39:00,517
Did you ever talk with her
on the telephone?

587
00:39:00,680 --> 00:39:02,796
- I told you no, I did not.
- That's right.

588
00:39:02,960 --> 00:39:05,679
You told me that time we met.

589
00:39:05,840 --> 00:39:08,673
You don't care for her, do you?

590
00:39:09,560 --> 00:39:11,118
No, I don't.

591
00:39:11,280 --> 00:39:13,635
- You know Doug Templitt?
- Yes, I do.

592
00:39:14,200 --> 00:39:15,918
He's a pretty funny guy.

593
00:39:16,080 --> 00:39:18,753
- How do you like his act?
- I've never seen it.

594
00:39:18,920 --> 00:39:20,956
- You haven't?
- No.

595
00:39:21,120 --> 00:39:23,270
Well, you're friends, aren't you?

596
00:39:23,440 --> 00:39:26,352
- More or less.
- What do you mean, more or less?

597
00:39:26,520 --> 00:39:29,239
He has his life and I have mine.

598
00:39:29,920 --> 00:39:32,036
Oh, how's your hand?

599
00:39:32,200 --> 00:39:34,555
It's fine, thank you.

600
00:39:36,080 --> 00:39:41,074
Where were you the night
Jason Hardiman was shot?

601
00:39:41,240 --> 00:39:42,958
I was with Doug.

602
00:39:43,120 --> 00:39:46,999
Well, let me ask you this:
Where were you last Friday evening

603
00:39:47,160 --> 00:39:49,754
when someone dressed
in a nurse's uniform

604
00:39:49,920 --> 00:39:52,434
went in that hospital room
and killed Jason Hardiman?

605
00:39:52,600 --> 00:39:54,556
Where were you then?

606
00:39:54,720 --> 00:39:55,709
I was with Doug.

607
00:39:55,880 --> 00:39:58,713
- So you were with Doug both times?
- Yes.

608
00:39:58,880 --> 00:40:00,074
Objection.

609
00:40:00,760 --> 00:40:01,749
Relevancy.

610
00:40:01,920 --> 00:40:04,354
Your Honour, it is entirely possible

611
00:40:04,520 --> 00:40:07,273
that someone other than my client
committed this murder.

612
00:40:07,440 --> 00:40:09,874
I have a right to pursue
that possibility.

613
00:40:10,840 --> 00:40:11,875
Overruled.

614
00:40:12,600 --> 00:40:15,239
Answer the question, please.

615
00:40:15,400 --> 00:40:19,029
- So you were with Doug both times.
- Yes.

616
00:40:19,200 --> 00:40:23,557
So you and Doug have been
spending quite a little time together.

617
00:40:23,720 --> 00:40:25,995
I suppose so.

618
00:40:26,160 --> 00:40:31,678
- Are you still back sharing now?
- Sometimes.

619
00:40:31,840 --> 00:40:33,239
Let me ask you this, Helen.

620
00:40:33,400 --> 00:40:39,077
If you were leaving this place
that you and Doug sometimes share

621
00:40:39,240 --> 00:40:41,834
and you were, say, in a hurry,

622
00:40:42,000 --> 00:40:45,675
do you think it would ever be possible
you might put on Doug's trench coat

623
00:40:45,840 --> 00:40:48,513
instead of yours by mistake?

624
00:40:49,960 --> 00:40:52,030
I suppose it's possible.

625
00:40:52,200 --> 00:40:53,792
You know, Helen,

626
00:40:53,960 --> 00:40:57,396
I've been looking at the tape
of that woman in that hospital,

627
00:40:57,560 --> 00:41:00,711
and it took a while
for the penny to drop,

628
00:41:00,880 --> 00:41:03,235
but I finally realized.

629
00:41:03,400 --> 00:41:07,837
You know, a man buttons
his coat left over right.

630
00:41:08,000 --> 00:41:10,230
A woman just the opposite.

631
00:41:10,400 --> 00:41:14,916
Now, the woman in that tape
buttoned her coat just like a man.

632
00:41:15,400 --> 00:41:18,039
And you know something else?

633
00:41:19,320 --> 00:41:21,675
You know that time when
we saw one another?

634
00:41:21,840 --> 00:41:23,990
You cut your hand.

635
00:41:26,120 --> 00:41:29,157
When I saw Doug yesterday,

636
00:41:29,320 --> 00:41:31,390
he had a bandage

637
00:41:31,560 --> 00:41:35,633
on the exact same spot on his hand.

638
00:41:35,800 --> 00:41:37,199
Now, isn't it odd

639
00:41:37,360 --> 00:41:41,956
that you and Doug would've cut
your hand in exactly the same place?

640
00:41:42,120 --> 00:41:44,634
Isn't that odd, Helen?

641
00:41:46,080 --> 00:41:48,833
I honestly don't know.

642
00:41:50,000 --> 00:41:52,309
You know what I think?

643
00:41:53,520 --> 00:41:58,036
I think that you and Doug are closer
than even you can admit.

644
00:41:58,200 --> 00:42:00,555
I do.
I think you're together all the time.

645
00:42:01,080 --> 00:42:05,437
I think that you're
somehow connected.

646
00:42:07,720 --> 00:42:11,235
I think we have a case
of confused identity.

647
00:42:12,200 --> 00:42:16,512
Let me illustrate my point
by telling a little story.

648
00:42:16,680 --> 00:42:21,435
One time a woman went in a barroom
with a duck under her arm.

649
00:42:21,600 --> 00:42:24,672
The bartender walks over and he says,
''Where did you get the pig?''

650
00:42:24,840 --> 00:42:26,034
The woman says, ''It's a duck.''

651
00:42:26,200 --> 00:42:28,270
And the bartender says,
''I was talking to the pig.''

652
00:42:28,440 --> 00:42:31,591
Duck. I was talking to the duck.

653
00:42:33,280 --> 00:42:34,269
What's this?

654
00:42:34,440 --> 00:42:38,115
You blew the joke. The bartender says,
''I was talking to the duck.''

655
00:42:42,080 --> 00:42:43,149
Doug?

656
00:42:50,720 --> 00:42:52,551
Is that you?

657
00:42:56,560 --> 00:42:58,755
Is that you?

658
00:43:00,640 --> 00:43:02,596
Doug?

659
00:43:03,520 --> 00:43:05,670
Helen said she was with you

660
00:43:05,840 --> 00:43:09,833
the night Jason Hardiman
was murdered. Is that true?

661
00:43:10,880 --> 00:43:12,757
No.

662
00:43:13,600 --> 00:43:16,637
Helen wasn't with you the night
Jason Hardiman was murdered?

663
00:43:16,800 --> 00:43:18,711
No.

664
00:43:24,200 --> 00:43:25,189
Doug...

665
00:43:30,920 --> 00:43:33,195
...who killed Jason Hardiman?

666
00:43:35,120 --> 00:43:37,554
She did.

667
00:43:38,200 --> 00:43:39,758
- She did.
- Helen?

668
00:43:43,080 --> 00:43:44,877
Yeah.

669
00:43:47,800 --> 00:43:50,837
I don't know a lot about this.

670
00:43:52,160 --> 00:43:55,675
I did speak with a doctor
friend of mine.

671
00:43:56,520 --> 00:43:59,239
I know that Helen is a part of you,

672
00:43:59,400 --> 00:44:02,836
and I'm very sorry to put you
both through this.

673
00:44:04,120 --> 00:44:05,599
One more question.

674
00:44:08,040 --> 00:44:12,352
Why did Helen kill Jason Hardiman?

675
00:44:12,520 --> 00:44:14,158
Why didn't she kill Carla?

676
00:44:17,120 --> 00:44:19,509
She wanted to.

677
00:44:24,360 --> 00:44:26,715
Carla was everything

678
00:44:26,880 --> 00:44:29,792
Helen wanted to be, but couldn't.

679
00:44:31,480 --> 00:44:36,110
She wanted to humiliate her,

680
00:44:36,640 --> 00:44:39,950
to degrade her,

681
00:44:40,880 --> 00:44:44,395
to take her son away from her.

682
00:44:46,520 --> 00:44:48,351
How did you feel?

683
00:44:52,480 --> 00:44:57,270
I wouldn't let Helen kill Carla.

684
00:44:59,560 --> 00:45:02,028
I love Carla.

685
00:45:12,920 --> 00:45:14,876
No further questions.

686
00:45:23,080 --> 00:45:25,196
Come on.

687
00:45:26,040 --> 00:45:27,029
Thank you.

688
00:45:27,200 --> 00:45:30,431
- Maybe it made up for the last time.
- It did.

689
00:45:30,600 --> 00:45:33,512
- Good luck.
- You too.

690
00:45:33,680 --> 00:45:35,591
Your father's not so bad after all.

691
00:45:36,200 --> 00:45:37,633
That's what he tells me.

692
00:45:37,800 --> 00:45:41,759
Remember, it's all in the shoulder.

693
00:45:44,240 --> 00:45:47,835
- What's in the shoulders?
- Professional secret.

694
00:45:49,440 --> 00:45:51,396
It's nice to know I have a trade
to fall back on.

695
00:45:51,560 --> 00:45:53,994
Charlene.

9999
00:00:0,500 --> 00:00:2,00
<font color="#ffff00" size=14>www.tvsubtitles.net</font>
